 If the area of the picture is {eq}\displaystyle 2 \ ft^2

{/eq} and its length {eq}\displaystyle x \ ft

{/eq} and width {eq}\displaystyle y \ ft

{/eq}, then

$$\begin{align}

x \times y=2 \quad \text{Eq.} (1)

\end{align}

$$

The length of the rectangular quilt is twice the length of the picture so the length of the quilt is {eq}\displaystyle 2x \ ft

{/eq}, and the width of the rectangular quilt is three times the width of the picture so the width of the rectangular quilt is {eq}\displaystyle 3y \ ft.

{/eq} Then, the area of the rectangular quilt is {eq}\displaystyle 2x \times 3y = 6xy \ ft^2.

{/eq} By {eq}\displaystyle \text{ Eq.} (1) \text{, this is equal to}

{/eq}

$$\begin{align}

2xy &= 2\times 2\\[0.2cm]

&= 4 \ feet

\end{align}

$$
####
The area of the rectangular quilt is 4 square feet.

